d inference monitoring tracks KV cache hit rates.\"\n\nYes, this maintains the technical terms and the structure. Let me double-check each term's placement and meaning.\n\n- \"cache RAG results\" – correct.\n- \"but cannot cross tenant_id reuse\" becomes \"do not reuse across tenant_id\".\n- \"微调只允许 LoRA\" → \"fine-tuning is restricted to LoRA\" or \"is only allowed with LoRA\". Both are okay, but maybe \"restricted to\" sounds more formal here.\n- \"推理监控 KV cache命中率\" → \"inference monitoring tracks the KV cache hit rate\".\n\nI think this translation captures all elements accurately. Let me make sure there's no ambiguity. For example, \"do not reuse them across tenant_id\" – does that mean each tenant has their own cache? Yes, because you can't cross tenant_id, so caching is per tenant.\n\nAnother point: the 10 minutes duration should be clearly stated. The original says \"缓存 RAG 结果10分钟\", which is \"cache RAG results for 10 minutes\". So that's correctly placed in the first clause.\n\nFinal check for grammar and flow:\n\n\"To reduce p95 latency, we cache RAG results for 10 minutes but do not reuse them across tenant_id; fine-tuning is restricted to LoRA, and inference monitoring tracks the KV cache hit rate.\"\n\nYes, this seems good. The semicolon separates two related clauses about caching vs. fine-tuning and monitoring. All terms are included as specified.",
